chapter.v:
And Solomon’s 


import of, 


horses was from Egypt and Kue, and the king’s traders would buy them from Kue for a price.

They imported 


a chariot, 


from Egypt for 600 shekels(3) of silver, and a horse for 150. Likewise through them these were exported to all the kings of the Hittites and the kings of Syria. Footnotes (1) 1:5 Or *him* (2) 1:13 Septuagint, Vulgate; Hebrew *to* (3) 1:17 A *shekel* was about 2/5 ounce or 11 grams (ESV)
